      "bookId": "the-uses-of-argument",
      "bookTitle": "The Uses of Argument",
      "author": "Stephen E. Toulmin",
      "category": "Psychology",
      "type": "mental-model",
      "headline": "The Probable Is Not a Weakness",
      "body": "Do not feel guilty that your arguments deal in probability rather than eternal proof. Weather forecasters, doctors, and tech founders all run on probability. A strong claim backed by good data and clear odds is the gold standard of real-world intelligence.",
